     1,
     "<font size=\"4\">Hi all, </font><div><font size=\"4\"><br></font></div><div><font size=\"4\">I am working with GGIR to process data on 24-hour movement behaviors. </font></div><div><font size=\"4\">When inspecting the part 5 output, I got pretty confused with the difference between the variables: </font></div><font size=\"4\"><span border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"217\" style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);border-collapse:collapse;width:163pt\"><span height=\"21\" style=\"min-height:16pt\"><span height=\"21\" width=\"217\" style=\"padding-top:1px;padding-right:1px;padding-left:1px;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;vertical-align:bottom;border:medium;white-space:nowrap;min-height:16pt;width:163pt\">ACC_day_VIG_unbt_mg  </span></span></span><span border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"217\" style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);border-collapse:collapse;width:163pt\"><span width=\"217\" style=\"width:163pt\"></span><span height=\"21\" style=\"min-height:16pt\"><span height=\"21\" width=\"217\" style=\"padding-top:1px;padding-right:1px;padding-left:1px;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;vertical-align:bottom;border:medium;white-space:nowrap;min-height:16pt;width:163pt\"><br>ACC_day_total_VIG_mg</span></span></span></font><div><br></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" size=\"4\"><span style=\"white-space:nowrap\">From the vignette, I understand that </span></font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:large;white-space:nowrap\">ACC_day_VIG_unbt_mg refers only to the time that does not fall into bouts of activity. In contrast, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:large;white-space:nowrap\">ACC_day_total_VIG_mg refers to the average for periods of bouted AND unbouted activity.</span><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:large;white-space:nowrap\">Is that correct? </span><span style=\"white-space:nowrap;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:large\">Could anyone possibly shed a light on this?</span></div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:large;white-space:nowrap\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:large;white-space:nowrap\">Thank you all in advance! </span><span style=\"white-space:nowrap;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:large\"> </span></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "lyC5q-BQAgAJ",
   "from": "Vincent van Hees",
   "author": "017566be30afa7f3",
   "date": "2023-11-01T13:41:08Z",
   "subject": "Re: [GGIR] Part 5 output variable names",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Hi Danilo,</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">ACC_ means that it is the average acceleration</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">day_ means that it refers to the waking ours of the day</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">VIG_unbt indicates that person is moving vigorous but outside any of the detected MVPA bouts, we call this unbouted behaviour.</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">total_VIG indicates that the person is moving vigorous at any moment during those waking hours regardless including both vigorous during MVPA bouts and vigorous outside MVPA bouts.</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Best,</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Vincent</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div>\r\n        On Tuesday, 24 October 2023 at 10:57 PM, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">danilod...@gmail.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">danilod...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br><br>\r\n        </div>"
    ],
